    "## 2. NFA: Non-Deterministic Finite Automaton\n",
    "\n",
    "An NFA can be in multiple states simultaneously. It accepts if *any* path leads to an accept state. NFAs are equivalent in power to DFAs (every NFA has an equivalent DFA), but often more concise.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Exercise: Convert NFA to DFA\n",
    "\n",
    "Given the NFA that accepts strings over {0,1} ending in '01':\n",
    "- States: {q0, q1, q2}\n",
    "- Start: q0\n",
    "- Accept: q2\n",
    "- Transitions: q0 -0-> q0, q0 -1-> q0, q0 -0-> q1, q1 -1-> q2, q2 -0-> q0, q2 -1-> q0\n",
    "- Question: What is the minimum DFA equivalent to this NFA?\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# NFA simulator: tracks set of current states\n",
    "class NFAEndsIn01:\n",
    "    def __init__(self):\n",
    "        self.states = [{'q0'}, {'q0', 'q1'}, {'q2'}, set()]\n",
    "        # State mapping: 0={q0}, 1={q0,q1}, 2={q2}, 3={}\n",
    "        self.transitions = {\n",
    "            ('q0', '0'): {'q0'},\n",
    "            ('q0', '1'): {'q0'},\n",
    "            ('q0', '0'): {'q1'},\n",
    "            ('q1', '1'): {'q2'},\n",
    "            ('q2', '0'): {'q0'},\n",
    "            ('q2', '1'): {'q0'},\n",
    "        }\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def accepts(self, string):\n",
    "        current = {self.start_state}\n",
    "        for char in string:\n",
    "            next_states = set()\n",
    "            for state in current:\n",
    "                for inp, targets in self.transitions.items():\n",
    "                    if inp == char and state in targets:\n",
    "                        next_states.update(targets)\n",
    "            current = next_states\n",
    "        return bool(any(s in {'q2'} for s in current))\n",
 "\n",
    "nfa = NFAEndsIn01()\ntest_nfa = [\"01\", \"001\", \"101\", \"010\", \"1001\", \"1101\"]\n",
    "for s in test_nfa:\n",
    "    print(f\"  '{s}' : {'ACCEPT' if nfa.accepts(s) else 'REJECT'}\")\n"
   ]
  },
