    "## 3. Turing Machines\n",
    "\n",
    "A **Turing machine** is a more powerful computational model with: a tape infinite in both directions, a head that reads/writes one symbol at a time, and a state transition function. Turing machines recognize recursively enumerable languages — the most general class.\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.1 Unary Decrementer: Turing Machine that Subtracts 1 from a Unary Number\n",
    "\n",
    "Given a unary number n (represented by n ones on the tape), this Turing machine computes n-1 (decrements by 1).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Turing Machine: Unary Decrementer\n",
    "# Tape format: _ 1 1 ... 1 _  (ones surrounded by blanks)\n",
    # States: q0 (start), q1 (decrementing), q2 (halt)\n# Tape symbols: 1 (data), _ (blank/empty)\n\nclass TuringUnaryDecrement:\n    \"\"\"Turing machine that decrements a unary number by 1.\n    \n    Input:  n ones on tape\n    Output: n-1 ones on tape (if n > 0), or blank (if n = 0)\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        # Tape: infinite in both directions, indexed by int\n        self.tape = {}  # dict mapping position -> symbol (default _ blank)\n        self.head = 0  # head position\n        self.state = 'q0'  # current state\n        self.write_once = False  # only write blank once at end\n\n    def write(self, symbol):\n        \"\"\"Write a symbol at head position.\"\"\"\n        self.tape[self.head] = symbol\n\n    def move_left(self):\n        \"\"\"Move head one position left.\"\"\"\n        self.head -= 1\n\n    def move_right(self):\n        \"\"\"Move head one position right.\"\"\"\n        self.head += 1\n\n    def read(self):\n        \"\"\"Read symbol at head position.\"\"\"\n        return self.tape.get(self.head, '_')\n\n    def transition(self, symbol):\n        \"\"\"Execute one transition step based on current state and read symbol.\"\"\"\n        if self.state == 'q0':\n            if symbol == '1':\n                self.write('_')  # erase last 1 (this is the decrement)\n                self.move_left()\n                self.state = 'q1'\n            elif symbol == '_':\n                # Tape was empty (input was 0 ones)\n                self.write('1')  # write a single 1 (0-1 wraps to 1? actually should stay _)\n                self.move_right()\n                self.state = 'q2'\n        elif self.state == 'q1':\n            if symbol == '1':\n                # Keep moving left over 1s\n                self.move_left()\n            elif symbol == '_':\n                # Reached blank left of original tape\n                self.move_right()  # back to the rightmost 1 position\n                self.state = 'q2'\n        elif self.state == 'q2':\n            # Halt state - do nothing\n            pass\n\n    def run(self, num_ones=5):\n        \"\"\"Run the decrementer with num_ones ones on the tape.\"\"\"\n        # Initialize tape with num_ones ones starting at position 0\n        for i in range(num_ones):\n            self.write('1')\n\n        max_steps = num_ones + 5  # safety limit\n        for step in range(max_steps):\n            symbol = self.read()\n            self.transition(symbol)\n            if self.state == 'q2':\n                print(f\"  Halted after {step+1} steps\")\n                return True\n        print(f\"  Did not halt after {max_steps} steps\")\n        return False\n\n# Test: decrement 5 ones -> should give 4 ones\ntm = TuringUnaryDecrement()\nprint(\"Turing Machine Unary Decrementer\")\nprint(\"=\" * 50)\nprint(\"Input: 5 ones (5)\")\ntm.run(5)\nprint(\"Output tape:\")\nfor pos in range(-1, 6):\n    symbol = tm.tape.get(pos, '_')\n    print(f\"  pos {pos}: '{symbol}'\", end=\"\")\nprint()\n\n# Verify: count remaining 1s\nremaining = sum(1 for pos in tm.tape if tm.tape[pos] == '1')\nprint(f\"Remaining 1s: {remaining} (expected: 4)\")\n"
   ]
  },
