   "source": [
    "## 4. Complexity Classes: P vs NP\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4.1 Class P (Polynomial Time)\n",
    "\n",
    "Problems solvable in polynomial time by a deterministic Turing machine:\n- Sorting, finding shortest path, linear regression, pattern matching\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4.2 Class NP (Nondeterministic Polynomial Time)\n",
    "\n",
    "Problems where a proposed solution can be verified in polynomial time:\n- Sudoku puzzle solution, Hamiltonian circuit, boolean satisfiability (SAT)\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4.3 The Million-Dollar Question: P = NP?\n",
    "\n",
    "Open problem: Is every problem whose solution can be quickly verified also quickly solvable?\n",
    "\n",
    "### 4.4 NP-Complete Problems\n",
    "\n",
    "If any NP-complete problem is in P, then P = NP. Key NP-complete problems:\n- Boolean SAT (Satisfiability)\n- Traveling Salesman Problem\n- Knapsack Problem\n- Graph Coloring\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# SAT solver: Check if a boolean formula in CNF is satisfiable\n",
    "def solve_sat_simple(clauses, variables):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Simple brute-force SAT solver.\n",
    "\n",
    "    clauses: list of lists, e.g., [[1, -2], [-1, 2, 3]] means (x1 OR ~x2) AND (~x1 OR x2 OR x3)\n",
    "    variables: number of variables\n",
    "\n",
    "    Returns: assignment dict {var: True/False} if satisfiable, None if unsatisfiable\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    n_vars = variables\n",
    "\n",
    "    # Try all 2^n possible assignments\n",
    "    for i in range(2 ** n_vars):\n",
    "        # Build assignment: var j is True if bit (j-1) of i is 1\n",
    "        assignment = {}\n",
    "        for j in range(1, n_vars + 1):\n",
    "            assignment[j] = bool(i & (1 << (j - 1)))\n\n",
    "        # Check all clauses\n",
    "        all_satisfied = True\n",
    "        for clause in clauses:\n",
    "            clause_satisfied = False\n",
    "            for lit in clause:\n",
    "                var = abs(lit)\n",
    "                polarity = lit > 0  # True = positive, False = negative\n",
    "                if polarity:\n",
    "                    if assignment.get(var, False):\n                        clause_satisfied = True\n                        break\n",
    "                else:\n",
    "                    if not assignment.get(var, False):\n                        clause_satisfied = True\n                        break\n",
    "            if not clause_satisfied:\n",
    "                all_satisfied = False\n",
    "                break\n",
    "        if all_satisfied:\n",
    "            return assignment\n",
    "\n",
    "    return None  # No satisfying assignment found\n",
 "\n",
    "# Example: (x1 OR ~x2) AND (~x1 OR x2 OR x3)\n",
    "clauses = [[1, -2], [-1, 2, 3]]\n",
    "n_vars = 3\n",
    "result = solve_sat_simple(clauses, n_vars)\n",
    "if result:\n",
    "    print(f\"SATISFIABLE! Assignment: {result}\")\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(\"UNSATISFIABLE - no assignment satisfies the formula\")\n",
 "\n",
    "# Another example: x1 AND ~x1 (contradiction)\n",
    "clauses2 = [[1], [-1]]  # (x1) AND (~x1)\n",
    "result2 = solve_sat_simple(clauses2, 1)\n",
    "print(f\"(x1 AND ~x1): {result2}\")  # Should be None (UNSAT)"
   ]
  },
